  "recognized_text": "Hey, thanks again for working my Saturday morning. So I'll do your Monday, right? Monday? I think there's a misunderstanding. I don't work on Mondays. We agreed you'd do my Sunday shift from 12 to 6. Oh. I was sure you said Monday. Sunday is difficult for me. I have a dentist appointment at 11. I see. But I really need Sunday because I have a family lunch at 1. What time does your appointment finish? At about 1 I could be here by 2. Then could you work from 2 to 6? I'll do 12 to 2 and go to the lunch after that. I'll be about an hour late, but that's better than missing it. Sorry about the confusion. Should we tell the manager? Yes, let's send her a message now so she knows who's working when. Good idea. So you do Saturday morning and Sunday from 12 to 2 and I do Sunday from 2 to 6. Exactly. Thanks, Tom.",
  "source_text": "Hey, thanks again for working my Saturday morning. So I'll do your Monday, right? Monday? I think there's a misunderstanding. I don't work on Mondays. We agreed you'd do my Sunday shift, from twelve to six. Oh! I was sure you said Monday. Sunday is difficult for me. I have a dentist appointment at eleven. I see. But I really need Sunday, because I have a family lunch at one. What time does your appointment finish? At about one. I could be here by two. Then could you work from two to six? I'll do twelve to two and go to the lunch after that. I'll be about an hour late, but that's better than missing it. Sorry about the confusion. Should we tell the manager? Yes, let's send her a message now, so she knows who's working when. Good idea. So you do Saturday morning and Sunday from twelve to two, and I do Sunday from two to six. Exactly. Thanks, Tom.",
  "source_turns": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "speaker": "Partner",
      "text": "Hey, thanks again for working my Saturday morning. So I'll do your Monday, right?"
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "speaker": "Learner",
      "text": "Monday? I think there's a misunderstanding. I don't work on Mondays. We agreed you'd do my Sunday shift, from twelve to six."
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "speaker": "Partner",
      "text": "Oh! I was sure you said Monday. Sunday is difficult for me. I have a dentist appointment at eleven."
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "speaker": "Learner",
      "text": "I see. But I really need Sunday, because I have a family lunch at one. What time does your appointment finish?"
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "speaker": "Partner",
      "text": "At about one. I could be here by two."
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "speaker": "Learner",
      "text": "Then could you work from two to six? I'll do twelve to two and go to the lunch after that. I'll be about an hour late, but that's better than missing it."
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "speaker": "Partner",
      "text": "Sorry about the confusion. Should we tell the manager?"
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "speaker": "Learner",
      "text": "Yes, let's send her a message now, so she knows who's working when."
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "speaker": "Partner",
      "text": "Good idea. So you do Saturday morning and Sunday from twelve to two, and I do Sunday from two to six."
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "speaker": "Learner",
      "text": "Exactly. Thanks, Tom."
    }
  ],
